[5] Structural identity (machine check on random reals):
    T[U,U'] = e^{-Ssp(U)/2} e^{-Ssp(U')/2} W(U,U')
    => T[U,U']T[V,V'] / (T[U,V']T[V,U']) = W[U,U']W[V,V']/(W[U,V']W[V,U'])   (spatial terms cancel identically)
    2000 random draws: max |lhs-rhs| = 5.96e-8  => identity exact
    Consequence: the Hilbert/Dobrushin oscillation bound for T depends ONLY on the 3D object W.

